{title: We Three Kings of Orient Are}
{key: Em}
{time: 3/8}

[Em]We three kings of [B7]Orient [Em]are;
Bearing gifts we [B7]traverse a[Em]far,
Field and [D]fountain, [G]moor and mountain,
[Am]Following [B7]yonder [Em]star.

{label: Chorus}
[D7]O [G]star of wonder, [C]star of [G]night,
Star with royal [C]beauty [G]bright,
[Em]Westward [D]leading, [C]still pro[D]ceeding,
[G]Guide us to thy [C]perfect [G]light.

[Em]Born a King on [B7]Bethlehem's [Em]plain,
Gold I bring to [B7]crown Him a[Em]gain,
King for[D]ever, [G]ceasing never,
[Am]Over us [B7]all to [Em]reign.

{label: Chorus}
[D7]O [G]star of wonder, [C]star of [G]night,
Star with royal [C]beauty [G]bright,
[Em]Westward [D]leading, [C]still pro[D]ceeding,
[G]Guide us to thy [C]perfect [G]light.

[Em]Frankincense to [B7]offer have [Em]I,
Incense owns a [B7]Deity [Em]nigh;
Prayer and [D]praising, [G]all men raising,
[Am]Worship Him, [B7]God on [Em]high.

{label: Chorus}
[D7]O [G]star of wonder, [C]star of [G]night,
Star with royal [C]beauty [G]bright,
[Em]Westward [D]leading, [C]still pro[D]ceeding,
[G]Guide us to thy [C]perfect [G]light.

[Em]Myrrh is mine; its [B7]bitter per[Em]fume,
Breathes a life of [B7]gathering [Em]gloom;
Sorr'wing, [D]sighing, [G]bleeding, dying,
[Am]Sealed in the [B7]stone-cold [Em]tomb.

{label: Chorus}
[D7]O [G]star of wonder, [C]star of [G]night,
Star with royal [C]beauty [G]bright,
[Em]Westward [D]leading, [C]still pro[D]ceeding,
[G]Guide us to thy [C]perfect [G]light.

[Em]Glorious now be[B7]hold Him a[Em]rise,
King and God and [B7]sacri[Em]fice;
Alle[D]luia, [G]alleluia!
[Am]Earth to [B7]heav'n re[Em]plies.

{label: Chorus}
[D7]O [G]star of wonder, [C]star of [G]night,
Star with royal [C]beauty [G]bright,
[Em]Westward [D]leading, [C]still pro[D]ceeding,
[G]Guide us to thy [C]perfect [G]light.
